*Ozone Profile Retrieval Control
SOMIPROF
Version 1.0.0
F                        ; do calculation at 3 VZAs (A, B, C), now disabled
F                        ; special radiance/wf interpolation, now disabled
F  F                     ; do_simulation, do_simu_rmring
T                        ; T: optimal estimation, F: Tikhonov regularization
F  F   F                 ; 1 T/F: 2 steps (2nd step for trace gas)? 2. T/F: both steps for trace gas?  3 T/F: large SO2 aperr
T                        ; T: fitting the weighting function of minor trace gases
* ATMOS, screen, intermed, gases, var., correl, covar., avgk, favgk, contri., residual, wfns, s/n,  ring,  ozcrs wrtalbspc
  F       F         F       T      T      F       T       T    F       F        F        F     F     F      F   F
* Filename for writing atmospheric inputs
INP/o3_wf_atm.dat
* do radiance calibration, type (1: climatology  2: true ozone profile from other souces)
F   1                           ; Next line provide the filename for true ozone profile
INP/tozprof.dat
T                        ; Use logarithmic of the reflectance
F                        ; Use logarithmic of the state vector
T                        ; use floor noise
T  F   F   F             ; on-line ring effect, slit convolution, fitting atan-1, KaiYang RRS table
F  F                     ; bias correction, time-dependent degradation correction
8  ; which biascorr (1: direct corr. 2: para. corr 3: dirrect corr (offset & slope) 4: para. (offset & slope) 5. same as 3 but LOG(I) 6. xtrack correction (theta) 7 xtrack and wave 8. time poly fit xwcorr 9 non-linear in time
/GOME/xw_corr_2008_poly2_nmls_25S0S_v4.0_nocali_varslit_asy.cor
INP/GOME_degcoirr_glb_lut_s_s6.dat
T                        ; do_subfit (T: some paraeters will be used for each window)
1                 	 ; 1: lcurve, 2: gcv, 3: gcv with lcurve
F       	 	 ; lcurve_write
0  0.05 1.0 0.000   	 ; PTR order, w0, w1, w2
3                         ; which_atm   0: NCEP 1 FNL 2 OMIMET 3 TMPOMET
13                        ; which clima 1: V8+EP  2: McPeters 8 TB 10 ML***** (see end for more option) *****
13                        ; which apriori error  1 Fortuin 2 McPeters   3. McPeters+GEOS-CHEM  4. MLS zonal mean 5. Ind. MLS precision
F  0.15  0.5             ; Loose a priori constraint, relative error in the stratosphere and troposphere
T                        ; T: update ozone below clouds through smoothing F: Don't update ozone below clouds
0                        ; which_toz Total ozone. 0: None 1: gridded TOMS/OMI) 2. Zonal mean 3. Individual (not implemented)
T                        ; T: normalize tropospheric column ozone F. normalize whole profile
1                        ; which albedo database (1: GOME from Kolemeijer; 2: TOMS from J.R. Herman 3: OMI from Omar, 4. Kleipool
4                        ; which_cloud (0 OMCLDO2/OMCLDRR; 2 OMCLDRR CLIMA; 3 OMCLDO2/OMCLDRR + OMCLDRR CLIMA) 5 Derived cloud from (O2-O2+RRS) : 3 default
F  F                     ; aerosol in LIDORT, stratospheric aerosols
* trop. aerosol (0: all 1: dust 2: sulfate, 3: BC 4: OC 5: fine SS 6:coarse SS), scale AOD, and aerosol optical thickness
0 F  0.01000
T T 0.80 20.0            ; Consider clouds, Lambertian Clouds, Lambertian cloud albedo, Default COD
F                        ; Cloud/aerosols T: asymmetric factor F: phase
63                       ; nmom: # of phase moments (start from zero, 0:nmom), overwrite VLIdort_control.inp
F                        ; T: use effectove cross section F: do radiance calculation at high resolution
0.05 0.01                     ; sampling rate for fine grid (must be multiples of 0.01 nm, 0.05 nm is good)
0.00                     ; small slit function
0.6 3.0                  ; sampling rate (nm) for Q/I determination (convolve, only used if polcorr = 6), wave exteded NEW
2                       ; # of spectral regions for specifying sampling rates
260.  340 910. 340 380   ; boundary of spectra regions (using different sampling rate in different region)
0.4    0.1  0.6  0.4 0.4   ; spectral sampling rate (unit: nm) to do radiance calculation
2                        ; Nstream
3                        ; which_polcorr, 0: vector only, 1: scalar only  2 scalar+LUP 3 scalar+pol,
T                        ; do_rtm_pca
F                        ; do_brdf

# which_polcorr
# 0: vector lidort, 1: scalar lidort  2. scalar lidort with LUP correction (removed)
# 3: VLIDORT at a few wavelengths and on line polarization corrections
# 4: Same as 3, but only in the first iteration
#IF vector lidort is used, you cannot use H-G phase function and g
#About the number of phase moments
#if delta_m is not set then [0, 2*NSTREAMS-1]
#if delta_m is set, then    [0, 2*NSTREAMS]
#
#which_clima (McPeters a priori is always used if not specified):
#1. V8+EP
#2. McPeters Clima
#3. McPeters+GEOS-CHEM   (both profile and standard deviation: 18 x 12)
#4. McPeters+GEOS-CHEM   (profile only 144 x 91)
#5. McPeters+LOGAN CLIMA (profile only 72 x 46)
#6. McPeters+zonal mean MLS (0.1 mb - 215 mb)
#7. McPeters+individual MLS / other profiles
#8. AB + TB + ML
#9  AB + ML
#10 ML
#11 geoschem_o3p by chris
#12 merra by kai
#which_a priori
#1. Fortuin
#2. MC
#3. MC + GEO-CHEM
#4-5 unused
#6. MLS  zonal
#7. Ind. MLS precision
#8. AB + TB + ML
#9  AB + ML
#10 ML

*ozprof
o3abs_brion_195_660_vacfinal.dat
